Reviews: Reviewer #1:
(3.5454545454545454, 'The performance of your submission is: 3.5454545454545454THOUGHT:\nThe manuscript specifies a sensible bounded comparison and carefully limits its conclusions to one reported quadratic evaluation. However, that singleton result cannot answer either central question: whether added polynomial terms help or whether regularization changes the comparison. All required sections are present, but substantial repetition and missing implementation details reduce presentation quality and reproducibility. The reported verification is attributed to host evidence; the supplied review material does not independently establish that verification. The rejection recommendation rests primarily on the incomplete experiment and limited research contribution, rather than on unsupported comparative claims.\n\nREVIEW JSON:\n```json\n{\n  "Summary": "The paper proposes a preregistered comparison of polynomial ridge regression across degrees 1, 2, 3, and 8 and penalties 0.0, 0.1, and 1.0, preserving fixed splits of 80 training and 64 validation observations. It specifies a fixed request order and selects among successfully evaluated candidates by validation MSE, breaking exact ties by lower degree and then lower penalty. The manuscript reports one evaluated configuration, degree 2 with alpha 0.0, with training MSE 0.00779644267729052 and validation MSE 0.007530714510483641. It provisionally selects this sole measured candidate and explicitly leaves the effects of additional polynomial terms and regularization unresolved.",\n  "Strengths": [\n    "The proposed grid directly separates degree comparisons at matched alpha from regularization comparisons within each degree.",\n    "The fixed splits, candidate order, selection criterion, and tie-breaking rules are clearly specified.",\n    "The authors carefully distinguish reported measurements from proposed evaluations and avoid inferring performance for missing candidates.",\n    "The interpretation correctly recognizes that lower validation than training MSE does not establish absence of overfitting.",\n    "The manuscript acknowledges validation-selection optimism, unavailable test performance, and the dependence of effective shrinkage on feature covariance and preprocessing.",\n    "All required sections—abstract, introduction, methods, results, and discussion—are present."\n  ],\n  "Weaknesses": [\n    "Only one of twelve planned configurations has reported measurements. Neither central research question is empirically answered: there is no higher-degree comparison and no positive-regularization evaluation.",\n    "Selecting the only measured candidate is mechanically correct but provides no evidence about model selection or comparative predictive performance.",\n    "The stopping point is insufficiently explained. The manuscript reports remaining CPU capacity but does not document whether the model-request limit or another constraint prevented the remaining evaluations. Remaining CPU capacity alone does not establish that further requests were permitted.",\n    "The contribution is an application of established polynomial regression and ridge-selection principles, without a new method, theoretical result, or completed empirical insight sufficient for a prestigious ML venue.",\n    "Feature construction, scaling, intercept handling, objective normalization, and solver details are unspecified. Referring to the host implementation without an accessible implementation or complete specification limits independent reproduction, especially for positive alpha.",\n    "The manuscript attributes the result to independent host verification, but the supplied review material does not include the underlying receipt or verification procedure. This limits assessment of provenance rather than establishing that the reported values are incorrect.",\n    "The abstract, introduction, background, related work, methods, experimental setup, results, and discussion repeatedly restate the singleton result and the same caveats. This obscures the small amount of completed evidence.",\n    "The literature discussion is largely synopsis-based, and the extended treatment of agent research workflows contributes little to the polynomial ridge question. Formal bibliographic references would improve contextualization."\n  ],\n  "Originality": 1,\n  "Quality": 2,\n  "Clarity": 2,\n  "Significance": 1,\n  "Questions": [\n    "What exact host resource constraint prevented evaluation beyond the unregularized quadratic? Please provide the request history and applicable model-request allowance so that adherence to the fixed order and stopping rule can be assessed.",\n    "Can the remaining candidates be evaluated in the preregistered order within the permitted resources, with every successfully evaluated configuration and its actual validation MSE reported?",\n    "What are the host\'s polynomial feature construction, training-fitted preprocessing, intercept treatment, objective normalization, and numerical solver conventions? Is the implementation or a complete reproducibility specification available?",\n    "What does independent verification check, and can the receipt supporting execution-0002 and its reported MSE values be supplied?",\n    "Why were there two CPU attempts for one distinct configuration, and what happened to the invocation whose metrics are unavailable?",\n    "If additional measurements become available, can the results explicitly report matched-alpha degree differences and within-degree penalty differences, while keeping conclusions descriptive and restricted to the measured set?"\n  ],\n  "Limitations": [\n    "The authors adequately disclose the most consequential limitation: the comparative experiment is incomplete and its central hypotheses remain unresolved.",\n    "Selection on one fixed validation split can produce optimistic estimates and does not establish stability across samples or populations.",\n    "Aggregate MSE values do not provide uncertainty estimates for paired model comparisons; the report appropriately avoids significance claims.",\n    "Undocumented preprocessing and penalty conventions constrain reproducibility and interpretation of regularization strength.",\n    "The narrow candidate grid, small dataset, and unavailable data-generating assumptions limit generalization even if the planned experiment is completed.",\n    "No concrete negative societal impact requiring special intervention is apparent from this bounded regression study. The principal foreseeable risk is overinterpreting a selected validation error as evidence of deployment performance; the manuscript already cautions against this."\n  ],\n  "Ethical Concerns": false,\n  "Soundness": 2,\n  "Presentation": 2,\n  "Contribution": 1,\n  "Overall": 3,\n  "Confidence": 4,\n  "Decision": "Reject"\n}\n```', True), 
